The solution may build on existing models and data, but it must bring clear added value to EDITO and its users.
The call defines innovation broadly. It may come from:
- developing a new application;
- integrating a unique or previously inaccessible dataset;
- reusing or adapting existing models in a new workflow ready for EDITO;
- combining several data sources or models;
- creating new user capabilities, such as what-if scenarios, early-warning services, operational indicators, policy-support tools or decision-ready outputs.
The innovation is therefore mainly in digital tools, data and their use for decisions, not in hardware. The first EDITO 2 call (closed in May 2026) onboarded existing mature solutions; this second call asks applicants to go a step further with ambitious developments.
